{
 "section_summary": "This section contains translated transcripts of Japanese shortwave broadcasts from November 1941, enclosed with two Federal Bureau of Investigation cover letters. The broadcasts report on Japanese–American negotiations, the emergency Diet session, evacuations, fighting in China and Europe, and preparations for war. Their commentaries portray the United States and Britain as hostile powers while asserting Japan’s commitment to an East Asian “Mutual Prosperity Sphere.”",
